## Installation

### npm

```bash
npm install {{ language.params.npmPackage }}
```

Import the modules you need. The package ships ES modules, CommonJS and TypeScript types:

```js
import {{ '{' }} Client, Account {{ '}' }} from '{{ language.params.npmPackage }}';
```

### CDN

{% if language.params.cdnPath %}
{% set cdnURL = 'https://sdk.appwrite.io/' ~ language.params.cdnPath ~ '/' ~ sdk.version ~ '/' %}
Every release is published to `{{ cdnURL }}`.

#### ES modules

Each service and helper is its own module, so the browser downloads only what you import:

```html
<script type="module">
    import {{ '{' }} Client {{ '}' }} from '{{ cdnURL }}client.js';
    import {{ '{' }} Account {{ '}' }} from '{{ cdnURL }}account.js';
</script>
```

#### Script tag

Add the script before any code that uses the SDK. It exposes every export on the global `Appwrite` object:

```html
<script src="{{ cdnURL }}sdk.min.js"></script>
<script>
    const {{ '{' }} Client, Account {{ '}' }} = Appwrite;
</script>
```

#### Subresource integrity

`integrity.json` in the same directory maps each `.js` file to its `sha384-` hash. Set that hash as the `integrity` attribute of the `<script>` tag, together with `crossorigin="anonymous"`.

#### jsDelivr

The script tag build is also available from jsDelivr:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/{{ language.params.npmPackage }}@{{ sdk.version }}"></script>
```
